[Term]
id: HP:0000005
name: Mode of inheritance
alt_id: HP:0001425
alt_id: HP:0001453
alt_id: HP:0001461
alt_id: HP:0010985
def: "The pattern in which a particular genetic trait or disorder is passed from one generation to the next." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
comment: While there is a close conceptual relationship between allelic requirement and inheritance, they serve different purposes; allelic requirement is necessary for variant annotation pipelines and to determine if a given variant in a specific context is relevant to the phenotype of the patient e.g. a heterozygous variant (in the absence of compound heterozygosity) is relevant for dominant but not for recessive disease; while inheritance is used for describing the mode of inheritance of a phenotype and is particularly applicable in the clinical setting for communicating recurrence risk, to guide family screening, and to guide reproductive advice.
synonym: "Inheritance" EXACT []
synonym: "Mode d'héritage" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission" EXACT []
xref: UMLS:C1708511
is_a: BFO:0000019 ! quality

[Term]
id: HP:0000006
name: Autosomal dominant inheritance
alt_id: HP:0001415
alt_id: HP:0001447
alt_id: HP:0001448
alt_id: HP:0001451
alt_id: HP:0001452
alt_id: HP:0001455
alt_id: HP:0001456
alt_id: HP:0001463
def: "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in heterozygotes. In the context of medical genetics, an autosomal dominant disorder is caused when a single copy of the mutant allele is present. Males and females are affected equally, and can both transmit the disorder with a risk of 50% for each child of inheriting the mutant allele." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Autosomal dominant" EXACT []
synonym: "Autosomal dominant form" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autosomal dominant type" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Forme autosomique dominante" EXACT []
synonym: "monoallelic_autosomal" EXACT allelic_requirement []
synonym: "Transmission autosomique dominante" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission autosomique dominante avec expression variable et pénétrance incomplète" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission autosomique dominante avec pénétrance réduite" EXACT []
synonym: "Transmission habituellement autosomique dominante" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:263681008
xref: UMLS:C0443147
is_a: HP:0034345 ! Mendelian inheritance
property_value: PROMOT:1000001 "Congenital myasthenic syndrom HPO DB associations" xsd:string
property_value: PROMOT:1000001 "Congenital myopathy HPO KB associations" xsd:string
property_value: PROMOT:1000001 "Oculopharyngeal muscular dystrophy HPO KB associations" xsd:string

[Term]
id: HP:0000007
name: Autosomal recessive inheritance
alt_id: HP:0001416
alt_id: HP:0001526
alt_id: HP:0031362
def: "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in individuals with two pathogenic alleles, either homozygotes (two copies of the same mutant allele) or compound heterozygotes (whereby each copy of a gene has a distinct mutant allele)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199]
synonym: "Autosomal recessive" EXACT []
synonym: "Autosomal recessive form" RELATED [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5316-1399]
synonym: "Autosomal recessive predisposition" RELATED []
synonym: "Autosomique récessif" EXACT []
synonym: "biallelic_autosomal" EXACT allelic_requirement []
synonym: "Forme autosomique récessive" EXACT []
xref: SNOMEDCT_US:258211005
xref: UMLS:C0441748
xref: UMLS:C4020899
is_a: HP:0034345 ! Mendelian inheritance
