[Term]
id: HP:6001011
name: Wet voice
def: "Wet voice is a perceptual vocal quality that is gurgly or liquid sounding and is due to the voice being produced through moisture. It is commonly used as an indicator of penetration and/or aspiration in clinical swallowing assessments and bedside screening tests." [PMID:25001523]
